load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A polygon: a closed figure of straight sides in the plane, the two-dimensional polytope. The regular polygons (equal
# sides and angles) are the faces of regular tilings: the pentagon of the pentagrid, the heptagon of the heptagrid, the
# triangles and squares of the 24-cell. In the hyperbolic plane a regular polygon can have any angle below the Euclidean
# one, which is why a right-angled pentagon exists there and tiles. The form carries the plane it lives in.
form polygon
  link plane, like vector-space
